        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Tascam 2400 = console + USB interface in one (replaced the Scarlett)&lt;br&gt;• Palmer merges the MPC 8-outs → ch 1-8; one MPC active per project&lt;br&gt;• Capture is &lt;b&gt;post-FX and pre-fader&lt;/b&gt;: the multitrack is a level-normalised archive, not a mix. The leveling is recreated at the mixing step&lt;br&gt;• Pass 1 = stereo master (the mix, every beat)&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Pass 2 = per-channel multitrack (only when a beat is picked up)&lt;br&gt;• DBX is &lt;b&gt;parallel&lt;/b&gt;, not an insert — the dry/crushed ratio is re-creatable later, but not recallable (it lived in the faders)&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Analog gear = sound modeling that cannot be changed. The DAW = mixing.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Mix and master are separate Pro Tools sessions — see manual_mixing_tascam_protools.md&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Line key&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;— solid = audio path&lt;br&gt;— red dashed = sample / re-sample send back into a sampler&lt;br&gt;— grey dashed = out of service" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1090" y="530" width="420" height="290" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

